- [ ] Live markdown styling in the editor (the big one)
  Obsidian-style inline rendering while editing raw text: bold/colored
  headings, styled `- [ ]` checkboxes, dimmed syntax marks (`**`, `#`),
  styled blockquotes and code fences. Means taking over line rendering
  from ratatui-textarea, so it needs a design conversation before code:
  scope which elements, and whether marks hide on non-cursor lines.

- [ ] Ship it properly: crates.io + releases
  Publish `mrkdup` to crates.io (grabs the name), tag v0.1.0, add a CI
  badge to the README, and set up cargo-dist (or a release workflow) so
  tagged releases ship prebuilt binaries for mac/linux/windows.
